I assume that when you try to sell something in the shop the shopkeeper 
wanders over, examines the goods, draws his breath in and mutters a few 
choice words about the shoddy quality before returning to his spot near the 
door and giving you a quote. The game short circuits this lengthy process 
and only shows you the end result, but you can be sure any self respecting 
shopkeeper has had a good rummage through your container before making an 
offer for it.

Of course, if this is what is supposedly happening, then there may be a 
possible bug should offering to sell a cursed BOH not cause some of the 
contents to disappear.

